# Complete table rows at span boundaries

The retained cq1-a28 mapping selected a numeric span five times. Duplicate validation rejected it. Its requested label ends the preceding span. The current focus recognizer needs a header and complete row inside one span. No source focus was offered.

The private evidence change adds one exact, bounded table window only for an unambiguous requested table row in one authorized source record. It starts at the measurement year before the column headings and ends at the requested row. The existing parser must establish the header, period, amount, unit and denominator from that same record. The whole window must fit 600 characters. It retains the original source identity, content hash and character offsets. It is an additional selection option. Existing spans keep their identities. No text from distinct records is combined.

Activation is restricted to the existing opt-in whole-span fact selection. The composer still selects the verified table unit. Duplicate evidence rejection and final safety remain mandatory. This changes the private catalog and mapping version. It requires fresh development evidence before qualification.

Implementation ownership covers a private table helper, its offline tests and the scoped composer call site. Sequential entry points and retrieval ranking remain outside this repair. The integrated source is already locally modified, so capture hashes before editing and preserve those edits.

Use different table facts for regressions. Verify boundaries, exact offsets and stable IDs, multiple records, conflicting rows, source hashes, unsupported branches, overlong rows, negative amounts and ambiguous labels. Replaying the saved failure diagnoses the old response. A fixed repaired response proves only the new engineering contract. It cannot change the failed qualification result.

No applicable generation allowance remains after the stopped CQ1 batch. Prepare a new two-case development protocol after offline checks. Owner review applies to future assessable drafts and exact stored approvals. The original batch remains one pass, one technical failure and eighteen unattempted cases.
